# Flow Overview

## Flow Name

`Operations Weekly Summary Flow`

## Flow Type

Automated cloud flow — triggered by SharePoint file creation.

---

## Step-by-Step

| Step | Action | Input | Output | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Trigger:** When a file is created (properties only) | SharePoint folder monitored | File ID, File name with extension | Use `(properties only)` version — not the deprecated trigger |
| 2 | **Execute Document Reader Agent and wait** | Message: filename | JSON: REPORT_DATE, SiteList, HyperlinkInventory | Set timeout to PT5M. See agent message format below. |
| 3 | **Compose** — strip code fences | lastResponse from step 2 | Clean JSON string | Agent wraps JSON in markdown fences; this strips them |
| 4 | **Parse JSON** — extract three variables | Outputs from Compose | REPORT_DATE, SiteList, HyperlinkInventory as typed values | Generate schema from sample — see schema below |
| 5 | **Set variable** — REPORT_DATE | Body REPORT_DATE from Parse JSON | — | Do not self-reference; use Parse JSON output, not the variable |
| 6 | **Initialize variable** — SITE_SUMMARIES | Empty string | — | Must be initialized before the loop |
| 7 | **Apply to each** — loop over SiteList | SiteList from Parse JSON | — | Set concurrency to 1 to prevent async hang |
| 7a | **Execute Site Summarizer Agent and wait** | Message: site name (Current item) | Site summary plain text | Timeout: PT5M per iteration |
| 7b | **Append to string variable** — SITE_SUMMARIES | lastResponse + line breaks | Running SITE_SUMMARIES string | See append expression below |
| 8 | **Execute Executive Summary Writer Agent and wait** | Message: SITE_SUMMARIES variable | EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY plain text | Timeout: PT5M |
| 9 | **Execute Appendix Generator Agent and wait** | Message: SiteList + HyperlinkInventory | APPENDIX_CONTENT plain text | Timeout: PT5M |
| 10 | **Populate a Word template** | REPORT_DATE, EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY, SITE_SUMMARIES, APPENDIX_CONTENT | Populated document (binary) | Template must have Content Controls — not text placeholders |
| 11 | **SharePoint: Create file** | Document Content from step 10; timestamped filename | ItemId | See filename expression below |
| 12 | **SharePoint: Get file properties** | ItemId from step 11 | Link to item (SharePoint URL) | |
| 13 | **Send an email (V2)** | URL from step 12; REPORT_DATE | — | Recipient: report distribution address |

---

## Key Expressions

### Step 2 — Agent message format
In the Message field of the Execute Document Reader Agent step:
```
A new weekly source document has been added to the knowledge source.
The file name is: [File name with extension — dynamic value from trigger]
Read this document and return the JSON output.
```

### Step 3 — Strip code fences
In the Compose step Inputs field (Expression tab):
```
replace(replace(outputs('Execute_Document_Reader_Agent_and_wait')?['body/lastResponse'], '```json', ''), '```', '')
```
Replace `Execute_Document_Reader_Agent_and_wait` with the exact internal name of your step if you named it differently.

### Step 4 — Parse JSON schema
Generate from sample by pasting this in the "Generate from sample" dialog:
```json
{
  "REPORT_DATE": "May 20, 2026",
  "SiteList": ["Site-1", "Site-2", "Site-3"],
  "HyperlinkInventory": [
    {
      "site": "Site-1",
      "displayText": "Weekly Dashboard",
      "url": "https://app.powerbi.com/example"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Step 7b — Append with separator
In the Append to string variable step Value field (Expression tab):
```
concat(outputs('Execute_Summarizer_Agent_and_wait')?['body/lastResponse'], decodeUriComponent('%0A%0A'))
```
Replace the action name with the exact internal name of your Summarizer step.

### Step 8 — Executive Summary message
In the Message field of the Execute Executive Summary Writer step:
```
Generate the executive summary from the following site summaries:
[SITE_SUMMARIES variable — dynamic value from Variables section]
```

### Step 9 — Appendix message
In the Message field of the Execute Appendix Generator step:
```
Generate the appendix for the following sites: [SiteList from Parse JSON]
Here are the hyperlinks to reinsert: [HyperlinkInventory from Parse JSON]
```

### Step 11 — Timestamped filename
In the File Name field of the Create file step (Expression tab):
```
concat('Operations_Weekly_Summary_', formatDateTime(utcNow(), 'yyyy-MM-dd_HH-mm-ss'), '.docx')
```

