## Variables Initialized

These variables must be initialized before the loop:

| Variable | Type | Initial Value |
|---|---|---|
| `SITE_SUMMARIES` | String | (empty) |

`REPORT_DATE`, `EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY`, and `APPENDIX_CONTENT` are set from agent outputs directly and do not require explicit initialization steps, though adding them improves debuggability.

---

## Loop Settings

Open the `Apply to each` step → Settings tab:

| Setting | Value | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Concurrency Control | On | Enables the degree setting |
| Degree of Parallelism | 1 | Sequential execution prevents async webhook hang |

---

## Agent Step Timeout Settings

For each `Execute Agent and wait` step → Settings tab → Timeout:

| Step | Recommended Timeout |
|---|---|
| Document Reader | `PT5M` (5 minutes) |
| Site Summarizer | `PT5M` per iteration |
| Executive Summary Writer | `PT5M` |
| Appendix Generator | `PT10M` (longer — reads all sites) |

Default timeout is `PT1M` (1 minute), which is insufficient for agents reading and processing large documents.

---

## Content Control Mapping

In the `Populate a Word template` step, map as follows:

| Content Control Name | Maps To |
|---|---|
| `REPORT_DATE` | REPORT_DATE variable (or Parse JSON body) |
| `EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY` | lastResponse from Executive Summary Writer step |
| `SITE_SUMMARIES` | SITE_SUMMARIES variable |
| `APPENDIX_CONTENT` | lastResponse from Appendix Generator step |

---

## Email Notification (Step 13)

**To:** Report distribution email address
**Subject:** `Operations Weekly Summary — ` + REPORT_DATE variable
**Body:**
```
The Operations Weekly Summary for [REPORT_DATE] has been generated 
and is ready for review.

Access the report here: [Link to item from Get file properties step]

This report was generated automatically.
```

